From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO Manga Image Finder

Find the chapter image of a tap in the manga mode picker more actively.
A tap now takes:
- the picture under the finger, also below transparent layers, unless
  it is a small icon, avatar or button (under 80 px);
- else the page image nearest to the tap inside the tapped element;
- else a page image right next to the tap (48 px) inside its parents,
  for taps on the gaps, page numbers and frames around pages;
- else an element under the finger that keeps the address of an image
  file (JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF, AVIF, SVG...) in data-src or a similar
  attribute, for sites that add their images later.

Page images are pictures of at least 80 px, or images still waiting to
load, that show or keep the address of an image file (or are loaded, or
are a canvas). A page still waiting to load counts with its frame, so
that it is found even while it is a dot. After picking, the reader also
waits for chapters whose images are not there yet.

